            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>A case of 40-year-old patient with compression of coronary artery and myocardial ischaemia is presented. Compression resulted from the herniation of abdominal organs into the thoracic cavity, which developed many years after the car accident trauma.</AbstractText>
